title: "Drawbridge — Frontend surfaces: what gets built, for whom, and how much polish it earns"
---
flowchart TB
  subgraph BUILD["BUILD — five surfaces, one Next.js app plus one docs site"]
    direction LR
    S0["<b>S0 · Judge entry</b><br/>the hosted URL, no login<br/>three doors: video, live review, docs<br/><i>polish: high · ~4h</i>"]
    S1["<b>S1 · Internal dashboard</b><br/>queue · timeline · gate · binder<br/>the screen the demo lives on<br/><i>polish: highest · ~30h</i>"]
    S2["<b>S2 · Vendor portal</b><br/>token-scoped questionnaire and uploads<br/>15 seconds of screen time<br/><i>polish: minimal · ~5h</i>"]
    S3["<b>S3 · Inbox simulator</b><br/>the mailbox that proves exactly-once<br/><i>polish: minimal · ~3h</i>"]
    S4["<b>S4 · Docs site</b><br/>overview, getting started, architecture,<br/>security, live demo<br/><i>polish: medium · ~6h</i>"]
  end

  subgraph SKIP["DO NOT BUILD — each one costs days and scores nothing"]
    direction LR
    N1["Auth, accounts,<br/>roles and org settings"]
